{"name":"Janna","hex":"#f4ebd3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Janna","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female given name from Hebrew, a fanciful modern variant of Jane."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Janna"}],"entries":[{"title":"Janna","blocks":[{"text":"Janna was a prominent Kannada poet in medieval Karnataka, India. He is widely regarded as one of the important Jain poets of the Hoysala period, known for his moral seriousness, philosophical depth, and refined literary style. He flourished under the patronage of the Hoysala king Narasimha I and possibly Veera Ballala II. Janna is best known for his classic Jain purana \"Yashodhara Charite\", as well as \"Anantanatha Purana\" and \"Anubhava Mukhura\"."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Janna","wikidata":"Q6155070"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Amrutesvara_Temple%2CAmruthapura-_Large_Stone_Inscription.JPG/500px-Amrutesvara_Temple%2CAmruthapura-_Large_Stone_Inscription.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Amrutesvara_Temple%2CAmruthapura-_Large_Stone_Inscription.JPG/1280px-Amrutesvara_Temple%2CAmruthapura-_Large_Stone_Inscription.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Amrutesvara_Temple%2CAmruthapura-_Large_Stone_Inscription.JPG/500px-Amrutesvara_Temple%2CAmruthapura-_Large_Stone_Inscription.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Close up of Poetic Kannada inscription composed by Janna on a Hero stone at the Amrutesvara Temple, Amruthapura, Chikkamagaluru district, Karnataka state, India","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmrutesvara_Temple%2CAmruthapura-_Large_Stone_Inscription.JPG"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Beige Chromography","image"